# Next.js & React Patterns

## App Router

- All routes live under `app/`; use `layout.tsx` for shared UI and `page.tsx` for route content.
- Use `metadata` export in layouts/pages for title and description.
- Prefer colocating route-specific components in the same directory or a `_components` folder.

## Server vs Client

- **Default to Server Components.** No `"use client"` unless the component uses:
  - React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, etc.)
  - Browser APIs or event handlers that require client JS
  - Third-party client-only libraries
- Put `"use client"` at the top of the file, once, for the component that needs it; keep children as Server Components when possible.

## Components

- Use functional components only.
- Prefer explicit types for props (e.g. `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>`).
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks in client components; keep server components thin.

## Styling

- Use Tailwind via `className`. Use existing CSS variables from `app/globals.css` (e.g. font variables) when relevant.
- Prefer utility classes; avoid inline styles unless necessary for dynamic values.

## Data and APIs

- Fetch in Server Components when possible (no need for `useEffect` + fetch).
- For API routes, add them under `app/api/`; return proper status codes and JSON.
